{
  "_comment": "The hot-run cases (tests/hot/README.md). Each submission folder holds one .xpi and one source archive made from a real submission by changing only package.json and the lock. `expect` is what tests/hot/check.js compares the work folder with: `stop` is `row-14` (the Build Review Details block), `abort` (the closing prompt of an aborted review) or `downgrade` (the question whether an aborted review whose XPI could be reviewed alone restarts as an XPI review). SCA_VULNERABILITIES and LLM_RESCUED_VULNERABILITIES name only the severities the case pins, each count exact or { \"atLeast\": n }. LLM_BUILD_OUTPUT is the folder the output lies in, always build, or false where the block names none. LLM_BUILD_XPI_MATCH is never named here: check.js prints it and compares nothing, since a case's lock is newer than the one its XPI was built from. SCA_ROOT is the folder the reviewed root lies in, sca or rescued. A rescued/ left in the work folder must hold no node_modules/. `reasons` are the early-exit ids of an abort or a downgrade, and `findings` the error findings the aborted review must hold.",
